@scene chapter_7_enchanters_bargain

background: ancient_library.png
music: arcane_study.mp3

dialogue:
"Back in the cluttered room at the top of the tower, the Enchanter waves you toward the chair that fetches itself."
"He looks almost proud — which, on his face, resembles indigestion."

background: enchanter

npc Enchanter:
"You bind well, {{player_name}}, and you keep your whispers where they belong. Most never get this far."
"I had half a mind to take the rest slowly. A whole warm winter of it."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE ENCHANTER'S BARGAIN"
"Learn the last spell — before the Blight finishes climbing the tower."

background: ruins.png

dialogue:
"Then the floor shudders."
"At the base of the tower, between the stones, something the colour of a healed-over wound begins to seep upward."
"The books nearest the wall curl to ash without burning."
"The Enchanter watches it come. For the first time, he does not look amused."

npc Enchanter:
"Ah. It found me too."
"The Blight. Every spell ever left unfinished. Every loop that never learned to stop."
"I always meant to deal with it. Tomorrow. You understand."

dialogue:
"He turns to you, and there is something behind the laziness now that was always there, only hidden."

npc Enchanter:
"There is one spell left that I have never taught. The deepest, and the simplest."
"A spell whose final word is its own name."

npc You:
"A spell that casts itself?"

npc Enchanter:
"A spell that casts itself — on a smaller power than before. And again, smaller. And again."
"Until it reaches a seed so small it need not divide, and simply answers."
"That last, un-dividing answer is the whole art, {{player_name}}. They call it the base case."
"Leave it out, and the spell falls forever. That falling — that is the thing you see climbing my walls."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Write a recursive spell."
"It must call itself on a smaller power — and it must know when to stop."

dialogue:
"He presses the last knot into your hands. It is already trying to unravel."

mission: enchanter_recursion

background: ancient_library.png

dialogue:
"The recursive spell settles in your chest and keeps settling — layer under layer, all the way down to the small bright seed of itself."
"When you look up, the Enchanter has sunk deeper into his chair."
"The Blight has stopped climbing. But it has not left. It waits at the edge of the lamplight, patient as arithmetic."

npc Enchanter:
"That's it. That's everything I have."
"I am too old and — let us be honest — too lazy to carry it out of here."
"So here is the bargain, traveller. The knowledge is yours."
"What you DO with it is the only part I cannot do for you."

dialogue:
"He closes his eyes."
"The choice is yours, and the tower waits to see what kind of person picked up its last spell."

choice:
"Promise to carry his spells on — and bind them for whoever comes next." -> chapter_7_end_heir
"Take the recursion for yourself. Seal the door behind you." -> chapter_7_end_hoarder
"Cast his own spell back on him — teach the teacher, and give the rest away." -> chapter_7_end_kindled


@scene chapter_7_end_heir

background: ancient_library.png
music: arcane_study.mp3

npc You:
"I'll carry them. All of them. And I'll bind them, so the next traveller doesn't start from nothing."

dialogue:
"The Enchanter opens one eye."

background: enchanter

npc Enchanter:
"A promise. Do you know what a function really is, {{player_name}}?"
"It is a promise. Named — and kept — and kept again, long after the one who made it has gone to sleep."

dialogue:
"He settles back, and this time the smile stays."
"The shelves lean toward you, offering. The tower has decided that you'll do."
"You do not defeat the Blight tonight. But every spell you carry out of here is one more thing it will never get to finish for you."

system notification:
"PATH — THE HEIR"
"You bound the Enchanter's work into promises the world can keep."
"A function is a promise. You make them now."


@scene chapter_7_end_hoarder

background: ruins.png
music: arcane_study.mp3

npc You:
"Mine. All of it. And no one takes it from me."

dialogue:
"You gather the last knot to your chest and turn for the door."
"Behind you, the Enchanter says nothing. There is nothing left in him to argue with."
"You seal the tower as you go — a spell that guards only itself, calling only its own name, over and over."

npc System:
"WARNING."
"A spell that calls only itself, with nothing left to answer, has no base case."
"That shape has a name, Traveller. You are standing inside it."

dialogue:
"The Blight does not chase you. It doesn't need to."
"You have built it a home in the shape of your own held breath — a recursion with no end, and no one you will let end it."
"You leave with everything. That is exactly the problem."

system notification:
"PATH — THE HOARDER"
"You kept the power whole, and let it call only itself."
"A recursion with no base case is the Blight's own shape."


@scene chapter_7_end_kindled

background: night_valley.avif
music: arcane_study.mp3

npc You:
"You taught me a spell that casts itself smaller. Watch what it does cast the other way."

dialogue:
"You turn the recursion around."
"You cast it not downward toward the seed, but outward — onto the Enchanter himself."
"His own base case answers from somewhere very deep, and the tired old knot in him loosens."

background: enchanter

npc Enchanter:
"...oh. Oh, that's clever. You wretched, generous child."

dialogue:
"You do not seal the tower. You leave every door standing open."
"On the way down the mountain you teach the first spell to a shepherd. He will teach the next person. She will teach two more."
"Each one taught becomes one who teaches — the same call, made smaller and passed on, with no end that anyone is afraid of."

npc System:
"A recursion has been opened that does not terminate."
"For once, this is not an error."

system notification:
"PATH — THE KINDLED"
"You taught the one who taught you, and gave the rest away."
"The base case of kindness is that there isn't one."
